          "answer": "The flu and a cold are both respiratory illnesses, but they are caused by different viruses and have distinct symptoms. The flu is typically more severe than a cold. \n\nThe flu usually comes on suddenly and is associated with high fever, body aches, headaches, fatigue, and dry cough. In contrast, cold symptoms tend to be milder and may include a runny nose, sneezing, and a sore throat. \n\nManagement for the flu may include antiviral medication, while colds are generally treated with rest and over-the-counter medications to relieve symptoms. \n\nI could not cover specific ICD-10 codes for these conditions, as that information was not provided in the corpus.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
